## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design a real-time, multi-tenant credit scoring pipeline with strong replay protection, verifiability, and auditability under streaming latency constraints.

## Key Concepts

- **Merkle proofs and verifiable data structures** provide tamper-evident audit trails
- **Per-tenant isolation** ensures strict data residency across Kafka topics
- **Replay protection** via sequence monotonicity and timestamp windows
- **Streaming windowed aggregation** and rollups for real-time computation

## Code Example

```javascript
function verifyDelta(delta, root, proof) {
  const validSequence = lastSequence[delta.tenant_id] < delta.sequence;
  const validSignature = verifySignature(delta.payload, delta.signature, delta.tenant_id);
  const validMerkle = verifyMerkleProof(delta, proof, root);
  return validSequence && validSignature && validMerkle;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This evaluates expertise in building production ML systems with zero-downtime deployments, governance controls, and operational observability.

## Key Concepts
- Versioned feature encoders and calibration rules for model management
- Canary rollout strategies with traffic splitting (typically 5-10% initial allocation)
- Idempotent update operations ensuring consistency and reliability
- Automated drift detection and monitoring for model performance validation
- Immediate rollback mechanisms for rapid incident response
- Per-user provenance tracking for model explainability and compliance
- Immutable audit trails supporting governance requirements
- Data residency considerations for regulatory compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for compute path
function computeScore(user, modelVersion) {
  const encoder = registry.get(modelVersion);
  const features = fetchFeatures(user);
  const encoded = encoder.encode(features);
  return scoreWithCalibration(encoded, modelVersion);
}
```

## Canary Scenario
Deploy version 2.0 to 5% of traffic, monitor key metrics for 30 minutes. If drift detection shows >2% deviation or error rates increase, automatically rollback to version 1.0. Otherwise, gradually increase traffic to 50%, then 100%.

